index 4479b53..72f852b 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,6 +2,38 @@
 
 This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
 
+## SMS sign-up verification
+
+Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and configure your Twilio Account SID, auth token,
+SMS-capable sender number, and `SMS_ORIGIN` (the exact public origin of the sign-up
+page, without the `/devtools-times/` path). For a deployed Node server, supply these
+values as runtime environment variables. Without them, sending codes fails with an
+explicit availability message; codes are never simulated or returned to the client.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint sends SMS using the
+[Twilio Messages API](https://www.twilio.com/docs/messaging/api/message-resource).
+Messages end with `@hostname #code` for origin-bound autofill. HTTPS is required for
+WebOTP in production; keyboard autofill, paste, and manual entry remain available
+when WebOTP is unsupported or dismissed. Trial Twilio accounts can only send to
+verified recipient numbers.
+
+Codes last five minutes, allow five attempts, and are consumed before registration.
+Resending invalidates the previous code. Sends are limited to one per minute and
+five per hour per session. Configure provider spending limits and deployment-level
+rate limiting by IP/recipient before public deployment, since session quotas alone
+can be bypassed by clearing cookies. Astro's session storage must be persistent and
+shared when deploying multiple instances.
+
+After code verification, the server forwards account details and the verified phone
+number to the existing external registration service. That service is maintained
+separately: enforcing verification for all callers and persisting phone verification
+on the account also requires that service to enforce the same policy. The local
+sign-up endpoint never accepts a client-provided verification flag.
+
+Run `node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/signup.test.ts` for isolated
+verification tests (mocked SMS and registration requests; no server required), and
+`pnpm build` to build the application.
+
 
 ```sh
 pnpm install && pnpm run start
